From: OpenHarmony PC team
Subject: [PATCH] kern/dl: keep loaded modules writable on EFI

GRUB 2.14 programs the memory attributes of a loaded module from its ELF
sections, but only for the sections that are covered by a GRUB DL segment.
Sections that are not covered - the .bss of the "relocator" module - keep
the attributes the firmware gave us, which is read-only on x86-64 EFI.

The relocator stores its boot state (grub_relocator64_rax and friends) in
.bss, so writing it faults with #PF (page present, write) and the legacy
x86-64 EFI kernel loader dies with

    !!!! X64 Exception Type - 0E(#PF - Page-Fault) !!

before the kernel is entered.  This GRUB is only used to boot OpenHarmony,
so skip the attribute programming and keep module memory writable.

Signed-off-by: OpenHarmony PC team
---
--- a/grub-core/kern/dl.c
+++ b/grub-core/kern/dl.c
@@ -654,6 +654,23 @@
   const Elf_Shdr *s;
   const Elf_Ehdr *e = ehdr;
   grub_err_t err;
+
+  /* OHOS: keep loaded modules writable.
+   *
+   * GRUB 2.14 derives the memory attributes of a module from its ELF
+   * sections, but only for sections that match a GRUB DL segment.  A section
+   * that is not covered by any segment - this is the case for the .bss of the
+   * "relocator" module - keeps whatever attributes the firmware handed us,
+   * which is read-only on x86-64 EFI.
+   *
+   * The relocator keeps its boot state (grub_relocator64_rax and friends) in
+   * .bss, so writing it faults with #PF (page present, write) and the legacy
+   * x86-64 EFI kernel loader dies with
+   *   "X64 Exception Type - 0E(#PF - Page-Fault)" before the kernel is even
+   * entered.  This GRUB is only used to boot OpenHarmony, so keep every
+   * module memory writable and skip the attribute programming entirely.
+   */
+  return GRUB_ERR_NONE;
 #if !defined (__i386__) && !defined (__x86_64__) && !defined(__riscv) && \
   !defined (__loongarch__)
   grub_size_t arch_addralign = DL_ALIGN;
